00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:51.190
<v Elna Baker>To be forgiven of sexual sin, I was required to tell the bishop. So while I often felt ashamed or humiliated in the room, I never questioned the process itself. It was routine, like going to the dentist. You turned yourself in whenever there was anything to report. And on top of that, once or twice a year, you were required to go to this thing called a worthiness interview.
<v Elna Baker>为了获得性罪的宽恕，我必须告诉主教。所以虽然我常常感到羞耻或屈辱，但我从未质疑过这个过程本身。这就像看牙医一样是例行公事，只要有情况就要去汇报。更何况，每年还要一两次被要求参加所谓的“配称面谈”。

00:12:51.190 --> 00:13:16.370
<v Elna Baker>Everyone did this, no exception, from the ages of 12 to 18. These were like checkups for your spirituality. The bishop would ask you a series of questions like, do you believe in God? Are you a full tithe payer? Are you honest in your dealings with your fellow man? In the midst of these questions about your faith, he'd ask if you obey the law of chastity. Reagan's first worthiness interview was pretty confusing.
