00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:43.770
<v Elna Baker>It took seeing them all together for me to realize how bad it actually was. There were stories of abuse on Sam's website. Some are extreme, like bishops who convinced children that if they masturbated with them, the desire to do it would go away. I was never physically abused, just asked questions.
<v Elna Baker>直到看到它们汇总在一起，我才意识到这有多糟糕。萨姆的网站上有很多虐待案例。有些很极端，比如有主教说服孩子如果和他们一起手淫，欲望就会消失。我没受到身体虐待，只是被问了这些问题。

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:58.410
<v Elna Baker>As a bishop, Sam said he never asked these questions, and he was never asked them as a kid. He found out about them from a friend whose son was asked about masturbation. Sam couldn't believe it. He posted about it on Facebook, and the stories came flooding in.
<v Elna Baker>作为主教，萨姆说他从未问过这些问题，他小时候也没被问过。他从一个朋友那里得知这些，那位朋友的儿子被问到了手淫的问题。萨姆简直不敢相信。他在脸书上发布了这件事，相关故事如潮水般涌来。

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:17.120
<v Elna Baker>Of his six daughters, four told him that they'd been asked if they masturbated. One of his youngest said she didn't know what the word meant. She was 12. So she looked it up on the internet, and this introduced her to porn. Sam thought if he brought all this to the attention of the church, they'd stop these explicit questions.
<v Elna Baker>他有六个女儿，其中四个告诉他她们曾被问及是否手淫。其中最小的一个说她不知道那个词的意思，当时她才12岁。于是她在网上查了，结果接触到了色情。萨姆认为，如果他让教会注意到这一切，他们就会停止这些露骨的提问。

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:43.190
<v Elna Baker>The church response was that bishops are not supposed to be, quote, "unnecessarily probing or invasive in their questions." But what's necessary and unnecessary is left up to each individual bishop to decide. The church doesn't define exactly where the line is. As the story got more heat, the church issued new guidelines this spring, saying kids could have a parent or an adult in the room when meeting with the bishop.
